# `break outer` is one edge from the comparison in the inner loop to a block outside both loops. No flag is set in the inner loop and none is tested behind it.
# The inner loop has two branches: the comparison and the counter. The index is checked against the length in front of the loop.
# CHECK-LABEL: in loop #{{*}} steps by 1
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK: Double b@[[element]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:TypedArrayElements
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isWanted]] = Equal(b@{{*}}, b@[[element]], {{*}}:StrictEq)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isWanted]], Terminal, {{*}}:StrictEq)
# CHECK-NOT: Upsilon
# CHECK: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# The patchpoint keeps the array alive and is no code. The length of the view bounds the iterations, so the loop does not poll.
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 5, patchpoints: 1, {{*}} steps by 1
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 5, patchpoints: 1, {{*}} steps by 1
